gpufetch displays information about supported GPUs alongside a
terminal logo.

The Intel backend is enabled for Intel integrated GPUs from Gen6
onward. The CUDA backend is an experimental, untested build option.
Users can enable it with CUDA=yes, including through sbopkg:

  sbopkg -i gpufetch:CUDA=yes

It requires the CUDA Toolkit with nvcc available in PATH
(or NVCC set to its path), plus a compatible NVIDIA driver.
CUDA Toolkit: https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-toolkit.
CUDA builds and NVIDIA runtime have not been tested here. Upstream's
selected CUDA architectures may not work with newer toolkit versions.

The default build has CUDA disabled. The v0.25 source does not provide
an AMD backend. The Intel backend was tested on Slackware64 15.0.

Builds use Slackware's pciutils and zlib. No network downloads are
needed during the build. Run gpufetch as a normal user.
